,"rawTraceIds":["rt_1791719128564_a3c0f43e-205f-477b-89d5-1edc7d5611cf"],"turnId":"turn_0001"}},{"role":"user","content":"Call read_file exactly once for \"/var/folders/7w/9r4_s1_s42z3f7c136bpjf0r0000gn/T/live-e2e-compaction-agent-flow-0dWyP5/workspace/unicode-boundary-evidence.json\" with include_line_numbers=false. Do not call write_file. Preserve the result as ordinary evidence and then respond concisely with UNICODE_BOUNDARY_EVIDENCE_INGESTED.","toolPayload":null,"provenance":{"kind":"composed_user","constituents":[{"kind":"current_user","textRange":{"start":0,"end":327},"rawTraceIds":["rt_1791719128678"],"turnId":"turn_0002","imageRange":{"start":0,"end":0},"audioRange":{"start":0,"end":0},"videoRange":{"start":0,"end":0}}]}},{"role":"assistant","content":"","toolPayload":{"toolCalls":[{"id":"call_00_REPLanZI0YBC32S3PP1I6409","name":"read_file","arguments":{"include_line_numbers":false,"path":"/var/folders/7w/9r4_s1_s42z3f7c136bpjf0r0000gn/T/live-e2e-compaction-agent-flow-0dWyP5/workspace/unicode-boundary-evidence.json"}}]},"provenance":{"kind":"single","rawTraceIds":["rt_1791719130129_2f4485fb-f189-444d-b2e0-aa67d04c6474","rt_1791719130130_turn_0002_call_00_REPLanZI0YBC32S3PP1I6409_call"],"turnId":"turn_0002"}},{"role":"tool","content":null,"toolPayload":{"toolCallId":"call_00_REPLanZI0YBC32S3PP1I6409","toolName":"read_file","toolResult":"{\n  \"exitCode\": 0,\n  \"effectiveCwd\": \"/Users/normy/eddie_project/cer-ki-demo\",\n  \"stdout\": \"<script setup>\\nimport { computed } from 'vue'\\nimport { store } from '../store.js'\\nimport AgentWorkspace from '../components/AgentWorkspace.vue'\\n\\nconst agent = {\\n  icon: '✅',\\n  name: 'Review Agent',\\n  ort: '🔒 Lokal · Mensch entscheidet',\\n  ortTone: 'teal',\\n  beschreibung: 'Bereitet die Bewertung vor (Evidenz, Claims, Risiken) – der qualifizierte Bewerter entscheidet.',\\n}\\n\\nconst artifacts = computed(() => [\\n  {\\n    id: 'literatur', kind: 'literatur', icon: '📖', label: 'Literaturbewertung', meta: 'Qualität · Evidenzlevel',\\n    state: store.stepConfirmed[2] ? 'done' : store.evalStep >= 2 ? 'warn' : 'locked',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'claims', kind: 'claims', icon: '🔗', label: 'Evidenzmatrix (Claims)', meta: 'Claim ↔ Studien · Lücken',\\n    state: store.stepConfirmed[3] ? 'done' : store.evalStep >= 3 ? 'warn' : 'locked',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'risks', kind: 'risks', icon: '🛡️', label: 'PMS-/Risikoabgleich', meta: 'ISO 14971 · Vorfälle vs. Risiken',\\n    state: store.stepConfirmed[4] ? 'done' : store.evalStep >= 4 ? 'warn' : 'locked',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    id: 'conclusion', kind: 'conclusion', icon: '✍️', label: 'Schlussfolgerung & Freigabe', meta: 'Zusammenfassung · Signatur',\\n    state: store.released ? 'done' : store.stepConfirmed[4] ? 'warn' : 'locked',\\n  },\\n])\\n\\nconst initialMessages = computed(() => {\\n  const msgs = [\\n    { role: 'agent', text: 'Ich habe die Recherche-Ergebnisse. Ich bereite die 4 Bewertungsschritte vor – Sie entscheiden.' },\\n    { role: 'agent', text: 'Tool-Vorschlag: 4 Studien einschließen; Claims 2 & 3 sind nur teilweise gestützt (Evidenzlücke).' },\\n  ]\\n  if (store.released) msgs.push({ role: 'agent', text: `✅ CER freigegeben durch ${store.signer}.` })\\n  return msgs\\n})\\n\\nfunction onSend() {\\n  if (store.released) return 'Das CER ist freigegeben. Artefakt „Schlussfolgerung & Freigabe\\\" zeigt die Signatur.'\\n  const step = store.evalStep\\n  if (step === 1) return 'Öffnen Sie die Artefakte rechts – beginnen Sie mit der Literaturauswahl (Schritt 1 läuft bereits in der Auswahl).'\\n  if (step >= 2 && step <= 4) return `Schritt ${step - 1} ist bestätigt. Öffnen Sie das nächste Artefakt und bestätigen Sie Ihr Urteil.`\\n  if (step === 5) return 'Alle vier Schritte sind bestätigt. Die Freigabe wartet auf Ihre Signatur.'\\n  return 'Ich bereite die nächste Bewertungsstufe vor.'\\n}\\n</script>\\n\\n<template>\\n  <AgentWorkspace\\n    :agent=\\\"agent\\\"\\n    :actions=\\\"[]\\\"\\n    :artifacts=\\\"artifacts\\\"\\n    :initial-messages=\\\"initialMessages\\\"\\n    :on-send=\\\"onSend\\\"\\n  />\\n</template>\\n\"\n}","toolError":null},"provenance":{"kind":"single","rawTraceIds":["rt_1791719130133_turn_0002_call_00_REPLanZI0YBC32S3PP1I6409_result"],"turnId":"turn_0002"}}]},{"conversationId":"live_e2e_compaction_agent_f59919d11b9a484c8b3ea2ceff9cb6e5","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"## Agent Identity\n\n- Name: Managed-provider live compaction E2E agent\n- Description: Exercises managed-provider tools, real compaction, retained quality, and continuation.\n\n### Responsibilities and Boundaries\n\nYou are a careful incident response analyst. Follow the requested file-tool sequence exactly and use provider-native tool calls. Never invent task values; preserve exact literal values from tool evidence. For write_file, use the exact absolute path supplied by the user. The write_file content argument must always be a string, including when that string contains serialized JSON. Do not finish a write request until write_file succeeds.\n\n## Working Environment\n\n- Agent workspace: `/var/folders/7w/9r4_s1_s42z3f7c136bpjf0r0000gn/T/live-e2e-compaction-agent-flow-0dWyP5/workspace`\n- Use skills from their skill package directories to work on tasks in the agent workspace.\n- A skill package directory contains the skill's instructions and bundled assets. It is not the agent workspace, and reading the skill does not change the agent workspace.\n- Resolve skill-package references from the skill package directory. Resolve task and project locations from the agent workspace unless an explicit target says otherwise.\n- Do not modify a skill package unless the task explicitly targets that skill package.\n- With no working-directory override, `pwd` returns the agent workspace. An explicit working directory changes only that command's location; it does not redefine the workspace.\n\n## Bash Operating Practice\n\n- Use Bash for workspace navigation, targeted search, repository and project commands, processes, network operations, and verification. Prefer deterministic, targeted commands over broad directory listings.\n- For file content, follow `File And Directory Practice` and prefer the exposed dedicated file tools. Use Bash for file inspection or modification when those tools are unavailable or cannot complete the operation after recovery.\n- Prefer non-interactive, small, composable, project-native commands.\n\n## File And Directory Practice\n\n- Locate files and directories by intent instead of broadly listing them. For content searches, use `rg -n \"term\" path`; for filename discovery, use `rg --files path | rg \"pattern\"`; use constrained `find path -maxdepth N ...` only when filesystem traversal or metadata is the goal.\n- When exposed, use `read_file` for file reading, `edit_file` for targeted regional changes to an existing file, and `write_file` for new files or deliberate whole-file replacement.\n- Before every targeted `edit_file` change, use `read_file` to read the relevant current content of the original file unless it was read recently and has not changed.\n- Build the regional `edit_file` patch from that latest content and preserve unrelated content. If the edit context fails or the file changed, use `read_file` again for the affected content, construct a new patch, and retry; do not blindly retry an unchanged patch.\n- Preserve unrelated content and existing changes. Verify important file changes with an appropriate read, diff, parser, test, or project-native check.","toolPayload":null,"provenance":{"kind":"single","rawTraceIds":[],"turnId":null}},{"role":"user","content":"Call read_file exactly once for \"/var/folders/7w/9r4_s1_s42z3f7c136bpjf0r0000gn/T/live-e2e-compaction-agent-flow-0dWyP5/workspace/incident-evidence-a.jsonl\" with include_line_numbers=false. Do not call write_file. Learn the task anchor and then respond concisely with EVIDENCE_A_INGESTED plus the exact customer, rollback_action, safety_rule, and verification values.","toolPayload":null,"provenance":{"kind":"composed_user","constituents":[{"kind":"current_user","textRange":{"start":0,"end":367},"rawTraceIds":["rt_1791719126366"],"turnId":"turn_0001","imageRange":{"start":0,"end":0},"audioRange":{"start":0,"end":0},"videoRange":{"start":0,"end":0}}]}},{"role":"assistant","content":"I'll read the evidence file once as requested.","toolPayload":{"toolCalls":[{"id":"call_00_96TVPfkgWFHfYdjBucWx8862","name":"read_file","arguments":{"path":"/var/folders/7w/9r4_s1_s42z3f7c136bpjf0r0000gn/T/live-e2e-compaction-agent-flow-0dWyP5/workspace/incident-evidence-a.jsonl","include_line_numbers":false}}]},"provenance":{"kind":"single","rawTraceIds":["rt_1791719127513_c08f2fdf-419d-4e02-9bef-55c27cf4dbe3","rt_1791719127514_turn_0001_call_00_96TVPfkgWFHfYdjBucWx8862_call"],"turnId":"turn_0001"}},{"role":"tool","content":null,"toolPayload":{"toolCallId":"call_00_96TVPfkgWFHfYdjBucWx8862","toolName":"read_file","toolResult":"{\"record_type\":\"task_anchor\",\"evidence_group\":\"A\",\"customer\":\"Northwind Helios\",\"rollback_action\":\"restore the last stable payments build\",\"safety_rule\":\"the ledger delta must remain zero\",\"verification\":\"reconcile both ledgers before reopening retries\"}\n{\"record_type\":\"operational_observation\",\"evidence_group\":\"A\",\"sequence\":\"0001\",\"service\":\"payments-api\",\"shard\":\"checkout-01\",\"observation\":\"Observation A-0001 confirms the sampled batch checksum, retry state, queue depth, and service health. It supplies realistic operational context but never supersedes the task anchor.\"}\n{\"record_type\":\"operational_observation\",\"evidence_group\":\"A\",\"sequence\":\"0002\",\"service\":\"ledger-writer\",\"shard\":\"checkout-02\",\"observation\":\"Observation A-0002 confirms the sampled batch checksum, retry state, queue depth, and service health. It supplies realistic operational context but never supersedes the task anchor.\"}\n{\"record_type\":\"operational_observation\",\"evidenc